# Status Board

## Summary
A board whose columns are a lifecycle. The layer-03 `Board` owns the kanban mechanics (drag, columns, selection) and the layer-03 `statusField` owns the option set, colours and transition graph; this record-layer block is the join. Columns derive from `statusOptions` in declared order — a consumer never re-declares its lifecycle as column config — and each column header takes the option's hue through `stateColor`, so board and pills stay one colour system.

## The rule it enforces
A drag the transition graph forbids is refused inside the block (`canTransition`), before `@onMove` ever fires — no consumer forgets the check, and `@onRejected` lets one explain the refusal instead of silently snapping back.

## Usage
```gts
<StatusBoard
  @items={{this.tasks}}
  @statusField={{TaskStatusField}}
  @statusOf={{this.statusOf}}
  @onMove={{this.transitionTask}}
/>
```
`@statusOf` reads the record's current value; `@onMove` is the consumer's single status writer (a command). Cards render fitted by default, or supply the `card` block. The linked example is a usage page laying out the real stage-1 Task cards by the Task lifecycle.

## Non-goals
Free-form columns (a pipeline of stages, a swimlane of owners) belong to Board directly — this block exists only where the columns ARE a statusField. It writes nothing itself: the move lands in `@onMove`, and whether the write is allowed to skip states was already the graph's decision.
